# GPS Toolset

Free GPS file tools at [gpstoolset.com](https://gpstoolset.com). Client-side parsing (no uploads). Clear · Private · Practical. Ads later via a central partial (off at launch).

## Environments

- **Dev:** http://gpstoolset.lan/ → `/var/www/gpstoolset/public/`
- **Prod:** https://gpstoolset.com
- `base_url` must be **env-aware** (detect host / env). Never hardcode prod URL for local.

## Docs (read these)

- `docs/plan.md` — features, rollout, hard rules
- `docs/cursor-prompts.md` — ordered Cursor prompts
- `docs/design-direction.md` — layout / tokens / `gpstoolset.ui.v1`
- `docs/seo-keywords.md` — keyword notes for tools + guides

## Stack

- PHP 8.4 · Apache 2.4 with `.htaccess` clean URLs (not nginx)
- Only `public/` is the docroot; `config/`, `includes/`, `docs/` stay above it
- No framework, no build step, no npm app bundler — plain PHP + vanilla JS + CSS
- Vendor libs locally under `public/assets/vendor/` (Leaflet 1.9.4, Chart.js, GoPro GPMF bundles, etc.) — no CDN for production pages

## Privacy

- All user-file parsing happens **in the browser**. Never upload tracks/videos to the server.
- No analytics / tracking beyond planned ads (ads off for now).
- Privacy line: “Your file never leaves your device.”

## Maps / OSM

- Tile URLs **only** from the central tile module (`config/tiles.php` + `assets/js/tiles.js`)
- OSM street tiles: `https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png`, maxZoom 19
- Visible attribution: © OpenStreetMap contributors
- No restrictive `Referrer-Policy` that strips Referer; no tile prefetch / offline bulk download
- Keep “Report a map issue” → https://www.openstreetmap.org/fixthemap
- **No contact email** (Paul) — attribution + report link only

## Layout (map tools)

- Full-screen map minus slim top bar (logo + menu). No permanent side panel.
- Graphs/stats/export dock **under** the map (map shrinks); resizable; persist in `localStorage` key `gpstoolset.ui.v1`
- Ads: central partial only; **never on map/viewer pages at launch**; max 2 when enabled elsewhere

## Design

- Tokens as CSS variables (teal `#115e59`, dark brand `#2dd4a0`, orange `#c2410c`, route `#0369a1`)
- Thin neutral borders / light shadows OK
- **No heavy coloured one-sided accent borders** (thick coloured `border-left` stripes)
- Drag-over = background tint (and/or normal border), not a thick accent stripe

## Hard content rules

- **No email address and no `mailto:`** anywhere
- **No contact page** and no links to one
- Never mention **FlySight** → say “GNSS logger CSV exports”
- Never brand as **“Telemetry Extractor”**
- GoPro / DJI = **compatibility wording only**; `/gopro` is the one allowed brand-in-URL exception
- `/gopro` copy must be clearly different from FlySync’s page

## FlySync / skylog

- May **COPY** client JS from `/var/www/skylog` (e.g. `gpmf-fast.js`, `gopro-telemetry-bundle.min.js`) into this repo
- **Never edit** FlySync / skylog files
- Do not copy Highcharts (commercial); use Chart.js or canvas

## SEO (every public page)

- Unique `<title>` + meta description
- Canonical via env-aware `base_url`
- Add/keep sitemap entry when shipping a new URL
- Clean URLs via `.htaccess`

## Workflow

- Verify at http://gpstoolset.lan/
- Commit after each prompt / logical step
- Do not edit `/etc/apache2` unless Paul asks
